      "problem": "| **$x$** | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-10$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nGiven the function table above, what does ${g}^{-1}(-3)$ equal?",
      "worked_solution": "From the table, we have:\n\n$$\ng(-1)=-3\n$$\n\nApplying ${g}^{-1}$ to both sides of the above equation, and using the fact that ${g}^{-1}(g(x))=x,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{-1}(g(-1)) & ={g}^{-1}(-3) \\\\ -1 & ={g}^{-1}(-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that ${g}^{-1}(-3)=-1.$",
